---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Google Play Production Access Questionnaire Guide"
  description="How to answer Google Play's closed testing and production readiness questions using verified engagement data."
  canonicalPath="/guides/production-access-questionnaire"
>
  <article class="card">
    <h1>How to Answer the Production Access Questionnaire</h1>
    <div class="tldr">
      <strong>TL;DR:</strong> Google reviewers check how you recruited testers, how actively they used your app, and what concrete changes you made from their feedback. Always cite real session metrics and specific fixes from your closed test.
    </div>
    <h2>Key questions Google asks</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>How did you recruit testers?</strong> Explain your community/platform cohort and opt-in flow.</li>
      <li><strong>How engaged were testers?</strong> Export your TesterLoop Markdown report showing 12+ active testers over 14 continuous days.</li>
      <li><strong>What feedback did you receive and fix?</strong> List concrete UI/crash fixes shipped in follow-up closed-track releases.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
